  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-27T00:59:59.778Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As I understood from last blog post by making \"veteran\" rank devs wanted to note players who not just trusted, but also very deep into vrchat. This is not bad, the only mistake was to make that note as part of trust level-ups and in result ppl treat this like top level that is should be achived as goal of the game or something like that. So it cause major misunderstanding in community. I specialy making this in \"feature requests\" to note this is not related to \"shield levels\". \n\nI guess I know another way to note creators and just active ppl in VRChat.\n\nThere is a russian reddit-like forum https://pikabu.ru/ this forum have awards for activity:\n- The automatic: https://pikabu.ru/awards ( https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=&sl=ru&tl=en&js=y&u=https%3A%2F%2Fpikabu.ru%2Fawards ) given for being intesting for other members.\n- And the individual: https://pikabu.ru/awards?mode=individual ( https://translate.google.com/translate?sl=ru&tl=en&js=y&u=https%3A%2F%2Fpikabu.ru%2Fawards%3Fmode%3Dindividual ) given for making ultimate hot topics, for just unusually creative posts or just for being initiator of local memes. It's shown in user profile (like this https://pikabu.ru/profile/0x00 ) and does not afect anything.\n\nJust imagine similar in VRChat: there is no color shining nickname that says \"look at this dude he is a veteran and it's cool, but we don't explain you why\" or something like that. You just see nothing specail untill you go into user profile in game or on site and see the small badges like \"this dude made The Great Pug\", \"This dude made avatar that >1000 ppl using\", \"this dude playing VRC from begining of Steam release\", \"this dude is a streamer that popularized VRC\", \"being AFK for 1000hrs\" and so on. If this badges will not affect anyting and will not shine on player's eyes every time and if individual awards will exist, then ppl will not be obessed with that and (mostly) will not try to grind it. But active plaers and content creators will be thankfull for acknowledgment and for small personal corner of glory.\n\nVRChat being \"first competitive social game\" as well as have \"social achievements\" is not bad, it's just should be presented correctly and should not psychologically press new comers or just regular players. And that's all.\n\nThere is alreay similar suggestions for that:\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/replace-veteran-rank-with-a-badge\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/community-helper-ranks\nAlso related:\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/trusted-content-creator-program",
